# NewUnera — Flow edge cases & outcome detail screens

**Scope:** Multi-step **action flows** under `NewUnera/` (Send, Add Money, Exchange, Get/Redeem CAD, KYC handoff, account actions) where users confirm a transaction and may land on **success**, **failure**, **pending**, or **under-review** outcomes.

**Canonical reference:** [`NewUnera/send-enhanced.html`](../NewUnera/send-enhanced.html) — `#step5` review edge UX + demo pills (~L2580–2628), `#step7` dual outcome wraps (~L2653–2730), CSS (~L2097–2207), JS (`updateReview`, `renderSendOutcome`, `buildSendReceiptRows`).

**Related:**
- Success hero (happy path only): [`.cursor/rules/newunera-success-screen-hero.mdc`](newunera-success-screen-hero.mdc)
- Receipt panel rows: [`.cursor/rules/newunera-success-details.mdc`](newunera-success-details.mdc)
- Review callout icons: [`.cursor/rules/newunera-review-callout-icons.mdc`](newunera-review-callout-icons.mdc)
- Wallet flow context: [`.cursor/rules/wallet-action-pages.mdc`](wallet-action-pages.mdc)
- KYC demo pill chrome (shared CSS origin): [`NewUnera/kyc-verify-new.html`](../NewUnera/kyc-verify-new.html) (~L346–358)

---

## Design intent

1. **Review step** surfaces path context (soft warnings), optional **blocking** edges before submit, and **prototype demo controls** to walk stakeholders through outcomes without backend.
2. **Final step** splits **success** (lightning hero) from **outcome detail** (error / pending / review) — same receipt density, different hero semantics.
3. **Stepper** must not show false success checkmarks on failure or pending terminal states.

---

## 1. Review / confirm step — DOM order

Inside the review `.card`, after summary rows and **before** primary `.btn-actions`:

```
.card
  ├── .summary-item × N          (flow-specific review rows)
  ├── .review-soft-warn          (path A — always visible, one active)
  ├── #reviewEdgeBanner          (path B — blocking; hidden unless demo / ?query)
  ├── .send-review-callout       (irreversibility + trust, e.g. 2FA)
  ├── hr.demo-separator
  ├── p.demo-label               “Prototype — simulate {flow} result:”
  ├── .demo-btns#…DemoBtns       (outcome pills — injected per path)
  ├── p.demo-label               “Simulate review blocker:”
  └── .demo-btns#…ReviewEdgeBtns (blocker pills — injected per path)
```

Use flow-specific ids (e.g. `#sendDemoBtns`, `#sendReviewEdgeBtns`) — pattern is reusable; names are not global.

### A. Soft warnings (always on, one visible per branch)

| Purpose | Pattern | Tokens |
|--------|---------|--------|
| Positive / instant path | `.send-review-callout` + `.unera-icon-lead--tone-success` | `--surface-fee-green-soft` callout bg |
| On-chain / rate context | `.rate-note` (flex + lead SVG) | deep-blue tint border/bg |
| Fiat / bank rail caution | `.dest-review-banner.cad` + inline SVG icon well | mauve-tinted `--brand-red` mix |

Toggle with `[hidden]` in `updateReview()` (or equivalent) from active flow branch — **do not** stack all paths at once.

### B. Blocking edge banner (demo pill or `?reviewEdge=` only)

Reuse **`.rate-expired-banner`** shell:

```html
<div id="reviewEdgeBanner" class="rate-expired-banner" role="alert" hidden>
  <!-- warning SVG -->
  <div class="rate-expired-banner-body">
    <div class="rate-expired-banner-title" id="reviewEdgeBannerTitle">…</div>
    <div class="rate-expired-banner-text" id="reviewEdgeBannerBody">…</div>
  </div>
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="reviewEdgeBannerAction">…</button>
</div>
```

| Behavior | Requirement |
|----------|-------------|
| Blocks primary confirm | `#confirm…Btn` `disabled` + `aria-disabled="true"` while active |
| Resolvable | Banner CTA refreshes quote, edits amount, or changes recipient — then clears block |
| Copy | Title = short problem; body = one sentence + next action |

Common blocker keys: `feeChanged`, `recipientBlocked`, `dailyLimit`, `bankLimitPreview` (extend per flow).

### C. Demo outcome pills (prototype only)

**CSS** — copy from Send / KYC; label ink **`var(--text-secondary)`** (not `--neutral-500`):

```css
.demo-separator { border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--neutral-300); margin: 1.25rem 0 1rem; }
.demo-label { font-size: 0.688rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-secondary);
  text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.demo-btns { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.375rem; }
.demo-btn { min-height: 34px; … border: 1.5px solid var(--border-subtle); … }
.demo-btn.active { background: var(--brand-deep-blue); color: var(--brand-white); }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .demo-btn { min-height: 44px; } }
```

**Markup:**

```html
<hr class="demo-separator" aria-hidden="true">
<p class="demo-label">Prototype — simulate send result:</p>
<div class="demo-btns" id="sendDemoBtns" role="group" aria-label="Demo outcome selector"></div>
<p class="demo-label" style="margin-top:0.875rem;">Simulate review blocker:</p>
<div class="demo-btns" id="sendReviewEdgeBtns" role="group" aria-label="Demo review blocker selector"></div>
```

**Two rows required:**
1. **Post-submit outcomes** — sets in-memory `sendSimulate` / `txSimulate` / `demoMode` (flow-specific name); always include **Happy path** (`null`).
2. **Review blockers** — sets `reviewEdge`; always include **None** (`null`).

Pills are **injected per branch** (path-specific labels); do not show irrelevant outcomes (e.g. “Bank rejected” on UNERA-user path).

**State:** in-memory only — **never** `localStorage` for demo outcomes (match KYC / Get UNERA CAD). Optional URL seed: `?reviewEdge=feeChanged`.

---

## 2. Final step — dual wrap (success vs outcome)

Terminal step hosts **two siblings** inside `.card.flow-card-animated`; exactly one visible after processing:

| Wrap | When | Hero |
|------|------|------|
| `#…SuccessWrap` | Happy path (`simulate === null`) | `.success-icon-animated` + `.lightning-badge` + stroked check — [success-screen-hero](newunera-success-screen-hero.mdc) |
| `#…OutcomeWrap` | Any non-success simulate value | `.outcome-icon-wrap` — **no** lightning badge, **no** success check animation |

Hide outer success CTAs when outcome wrap shows: `#…SuccessActions[hidden] { display: none !important; }`.

### Outcome detail layout (required order)

```
.send-outcome-screen[role="region"][aria-live="polite"]
  ├── .outcome-icon-wrap.outcome-icon-wrap--{error|review|pending}
  ├── .outcome-badge.outcome-badge--{error|review|pending}   (optional pill)
  ├── h2.send-outcome-title#…OutcomeTitle[tabindex="-1"]
  ├── .send-outcome-amount.send-outcome-amount--{neutral|error|pending}
  ├── p.send-outcome-sub
  ├── .error-ref-chip                              (optional; monospace ref)
  ├── .success-details#…OutcomeDetails             ← same panel as success — [success-details](newunera-success-details.mdc)
  ├── p.outcome-tip[role="note"]                   (retry / compliance guidance)
  └── .btn-actions#…OutcomeActions                 (contextual CTAs inside wrap)
```

### Icon & status semantics

| State | Icon wrap | Badge | Amount color | Status row color |
|-------|-----------|-------|--------------|------------------|
| Failed / cancelled | `--error` tint | `--error` | `--error` or `--text-primary` | `var(--error)` |
| Under review | `--review` / warning tint | `--review` | `--text-primary` | `var(--warning)` |
| Pending settlement | `--pending` / light-blue tint | `--pending` | `var(--brand-purple)` | `var(--brand-purple)` or `var(--warning)` |
| Completed (happy) | success hero | — | `var(--fin-up)` | `var(--success)` |

Icons: inline Material SVG, `fill="currentColor"`, 40×40 inside 100×100 circle — see `OUTCOME_ICONS` in Send script.

### Receipt panel

Populate via shared helper (e.g. `buildSendReceiptRows(txId)`) used by **both** success and outcome paths. Minimum rows: flow-specific fields + **Transaction ID**, **Date & time**, **Status**. Do not duplicate row logic in separate renderers.

### CTAs by outcome class

| Class | Primary | Secondary |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| Safe retry (wallet rejected, burn reverted) | Try again → review or amount step | View Wallet |
| User fix (limit, invalid recipient) | Edit amount / Change recipient | View Wallet |
| Hard block / partial (support) | Contact support | View Wallet |
| Pending / compliance | View Wallet | Send again / New {action} |

Copy must distinguish **wallet rejected** (user cancelled) vs **on-chain failed** (network revert) vs **pending settlement** (funds in flight).

### Follow-up copy

- Retry-safe: `p.input-hint--success-followup` pattern optional under hero amount on success; on outcomes prefer **`.outcome-tip`** with lightbulb SVG + `<strong>Tip:</strong>`.
- Pending: include settlement window (e.g. “1–3 business days”) in subcopy and/or a detail row.

